{"id": "EUVD-2026-67490", "enisaUuid": "4e49b9d8-9642-3497-a027-4ca9199052e8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: emac: Fix NULL pointer dereference in emac_probe\n\nMove devm_request_irq() after devm_platform_ioremap_resource() so that\ndev->emacp is mapped before the interrupt handler can fire.  An early\ninterrupt hitting emac_irq() would dereference the NULL dev->emacp and\ncrash.\n\nAlso remove redundant error message. devm_platform_ioremap_resource()\nalready returns an error message with dev_err_probe().", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:48:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:34", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90bb7164878b5e57d447f02c71c238f4f246016a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a103cdb0681e7185d1b0a12ce6a7c5416c208ccd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44068b6863fbda78fc810921ddf61642c377b3ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f623d38fe6c4e8c40b23f42cc6fe6963fa49997b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-72vm-9gwv-cwmm", "CVE-2026-80614"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a5a5525-8ae4-3a7a-89c2-f2d327416863", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dcc34ef7c83473222027f475014a2bf8ab798372 <44068b6863fbda78fc810921ddf61642c377b3ca"}, {"id": "1c517b64-f8e8-34e9-ab11-4f348ca99194", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "2d0327a1-344f-3cc1-ac9b-31b1c6d920de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "376ac408-fc37-3aa1-b01b-ff320af8a766", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "39e48917-122a-32fb-933b-f6bb4b67396e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "3c59b136-9c86-345